{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Stormbringer: Lightning Rod spreads Volt from Forked Lightning damage (#1681)",
  "contract": "#1681 Lightning Rod (300609) is SPELL_ATTR0_PASSIVE with ProcChance 15, Spell.dbc ProcFlags 0 and one effect: SPELL_EFFECT_APPLY_AURA with EffectApplyAuraName 42 (SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL) on EffectTriggerSpell 300928. Two independent dead ends stopped it. With no spell_proc row, SpellMgr::LoadSpellProcs skipped the record ('Skip if no proc flags in DBC') and Aura::GetProcEffectMask returned 0 ('only auras with spell proc entry can trigger proc'), so the 15% roll never happened; and 300928's only effect is 169 (SPELL_EFFECT_ASCENSION_SPREAD_AURA), which this core binds to Spell::EffectNULL, so even a restored proc would have done nothing. The fix therefore performs the roll and the spread in the module, in the class's existing AllSpellScript OnSpellHitResult hook, which already runs a chance-on-direct-damage proc for Electrocutioner. The roll reuses that same arithmetic - the talent's own ProcChance plus one point per five stacks of Static 803102, which is what 'Chance increases based on Static level' means - so at 100 Static the chance is 15 + 20 = 35 per Forked Lightning hit. The spread copies 300928's own DBC row: MaxAffectedTargets 1 enemies inside EffectRadiusIndex 14 (SpellRadius.dbc 14 = 8.0 yards), receiving a copy of the caster's Volt (EffectTriggerSpell 500928, DurationIndex 85 = 18000 ms) with its stacks, remaining duration and per-effect amounts, the same helper shape AscensionPyromancer::Spread uses and the same idiom as its call site, which takes the count and the radius from the spread spell's own record. Forked Lightning 801851 is the trigger (SpellFamilyName 22, DmgClass 1, first spell of its rank chain). The discriminator is the presence of the caster's Volt on an enemy that was never a Volt target and is not reachable by any other path; it reads absent on the current binary. The scenario deliberately asserts no damage number, and it does not assert a proc rate, which the harness cannot measure. OPEN: 300928 carries both EffectMiscValue 5 and MaxAffectedTargets 1 while the tooltip says 'each affected enemy'. The implementation follows MaxAffectedTargets because that is what the analogous call site reads; which field the original server used is unresolved.",
